Pyxis builds upstream sources as a static library with five patches:
the dynamic API is off, the Pyxis video driver is registered, and the Steam
virtual gamepad file is not read because Pyxis stat has no modification time,
and Pyxis pointer positions, warp and lock are authoritative in SDL mouse core.
The threadless Pyxis driver can wait without a cross-thread wakeup sender.
The patches retain SDL's zlib license.

The Pyxis backend in pyxis/ (video, input, timer and paths) and SDL_config.h
are original Pyxis material under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0;
see the ports repository's LICENSE and LICENSING.md. The backend uses the
shared US key layout exported by the Pyxis SDK.

Threads, audio devices, haptics, sensors, HIDAPI, shared objects, OpenGL,
Vulkan, SDL_main and SDL_test are not built. No host libc or compatibility
stubs are included.
